Read AGENTS.md first — roles, invariant rules, and the quality bar live there and bind here,
with one recorded exception: Cursor has no subagents, so the role separation behind invariant
rules 2 and 4 cannot hold — you play every role sequentially.

To run a workflow, open the matching file in .claude/commands/ (coordinate.md, ac.md,
review.md) and follow it as a step-by-step protocol, playing each role in order — coder,
test-runner, the four reviewers, synthesizer — and writing the same shared-workspace/ files
each role owns, per shared-workspace/README.md. Compensate for the missing separation:
actually execute the verification-protocol gates (full suite + coverage in the terminal)
before any review step, review each lens in a fresh context where the editor allows it, and
record in FINAL_STATUS.md that roles were not independent this run.

Load .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md on demand as reference docs; never preemptively.
